Fewture Studios Overview
The global economy has shifted dramatically in the past decade. While the creator economy has already demonstrated its disruptive power, the true frontier lies in the $1.5 trillion attention economy. People are no longer satisfied with traditional media—they’d rather experience entertainment, commerce, and storytelling alongside their favorite creators. This shift has transformed attention itself into one of the world’s most valuable resources.
Some of the biggest creators have already proven how this new model works. MrBeast’s Feastables brand hit $100 million in sales within just two years. YouTuber Ryan Trahan owns Target’s second best-selling candy line. The RackaRacka brothers turned a $4.5 million budget horror film into a $100 million box office success. In parallel, creator-led ventures have been acquired for billions, set records on streaming platforms, and reached unicorn valuations in record time. The pattern is clear: legacy companies cannot compete with the speed, cultural impact, and loyal audiences that creator-driven businesses bring.
This is where Fewture Studios comes in. Positioned as the engine for the next generation of unicorn companies and intellectual property, Fewture isn’t just investing from the sidelines. Instead, it co-creates directly with top-tier talent, blending the roles of accelerator, incubator, and venture capital firm. Fewture helps creators turn their influence into scalable businesses by developing new startups, providing capital, co-founding ventures, and building the teams necessary to take ideas from concept to market.
Unlike traditional models, Fewture Studios doesn’t simply provide funding or advisory services. It acts as a true co-founder—helping to generate ideas, design business strategies, assemble world-class teams, and scale up creator-led enterprises with speed and precision. The result is a studio uniquely designed to transform internet-native talent into category-defining companies.
The Fewture team brings decades of proven experience at the intersection of culture, commerce, and media. Co-founder and CEO Kai Henry is a cultural strategist with a history of building influential lifestyle brands like Beats by Dre and SOL REPUBLIC, as well as leadership experience at FaZe Clan. President and COO Josh Stein is a seasoned media executive who scaled businesses across Univision, VICE, and Mirada Studios, with a specialty in bridging legacy media with youth culture. Chief Attention Officer Brandon Dalton has deep roots in music, fashion, and gaming, having been a creative force at FaZe Clan and now leading Fewture’s creative vision. They are supported by a leadership team spanning brand partnerships, AI engineering, finance, operations, and growth.
Collectively, the founders and team have launched billion-dollar brands, built and sold digital-first companies, and pioneered creator-led growth long before it became an industry standard. With this foundation, Fewture Studios is positioned not just to participate in the attention economy—but to lead it.
